// ============================================================================
// Payment Gateway Platform — Base Application Configuration
// ============================================================================
// This file defines ONLY the application shell (Chunk 0 / bootstrap). It
// deliberately carries no entities of its own — entities live in the
// numbered files alongside it (10-tenant.jdl, 20-catalog-fx.jdl, etc.) and
// are merged in at generation time by passing every file to the same
// `jhipster jdl` invocation. See ../docs/TASK_BREAKDOWN.md, Chunk 0, for the
// exact command and the review/test/commit steps around it.
//
// Decisions baked in here were made explicitly with the project owner
// (2026-09-21): monolith first (not a microservices skeleton yet), Angular
// admin client, JWT auth for internal/staff accounts, Maven build. See
// ../docs/adr-jhipster.md for the full reasoning — this config is the
// direct implementation of that ADR's "Decision" and "Next Steps" sections.
//
// Rename baseName / packageName here before running anything if the
// assumed names below aren't what you want — it's far cheaper to change
// now than after entities exist.
// ============================================================================

application {
  config {
    baseName paymentgateway
    packageName io.paymentgateway.core
    applicationType monolith
    authenticationType jwt
    buildTool maven
    cacheProvider caffeine
    clientFramework angular
    databaseType sql
    devDatabaseType postgresql
    prodDatabaseType postgresql
    dtoSuffix DTO
    enableHibernateCache true
    enableSwaggerCodegen true
    enableTranslation false
    jhiPrefix jhi
    languages [en]
    messageBroker false
    nativeLanguage en
    reactive false
    searchEngine false
    serverPort 8080
    serviceDiscoveryType false
    skipUserManagement false
    testFrameworks [cypress, cucumber]
    websocket false
    withAdminUi true
  }
  entities *
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Notes for whoever runs this (human or Claude Code):
//
// 1. devDatabaseType is set to postgresql, not the JHipster default h2,
//    because the row-level-security tenant-isolation layer (Chunk 5 in the
//    task breakdown) can only be developed and tested against real
//    Postgres — H2 doesn't support RLS. Requires a local/dev Postgres
//    instance from day one; docker-compose for it is part of Chunk 0's
//    deliverables.
//
// 2. messageBroker is off here. Kafka is introduced deliberately later, at
//    the point the ADR's Chunk 10 migration roadmap calls for it (Phase 2:
//    extracting Transaction & Routing once throughput exceeds ~1,000
//    writes/sec) — not before there's a service boundary that needs it.
//
// 3. skipUserManagement is false: JHipster's generated User/Authority
//    entities back the INTERNAL staff/admin login only. The merchant-facing
//    API-key authentication (sk_live_..., sk_test_...) described in the
//    spec's Chunk 10 is unrelated and is built by hand in the Transaction
//    module — do not try to unify these two auth systems.
//
// 4. serviceDiscoveryType is false because this is a monolith. When Chunk
//    10's roadmap phase 2/3 extraction actually happens, this file gets a
//    follow-up revision (applicationType microservice, serviceDiscoveryType
//    consul, messageBroker kafka) — that is future work, not part of this
//    generation.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
